<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dingjiazhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1275</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-conquest-of-the-song-dynasty">Mongol conquest of the Song dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dingjiazhou was fought in 1275 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze River</a> between the Mongol forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> army commanded by Jia Sidao. The Song army collapsed. The defeat opened the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> to advance on the Song capital and led to the fall of the Song Dynasty.</p></div>
